In rectangle $ABCD$, $AD=1$, $P$ is on $\overline{AB}$, and $\overline{DB}$ and $\overline{DP}$ trisect $\angle ADC$. Write the perimeter of $\triangle BDP$ in simplest form as:  $w + \frac{x \cdot \sqrt{y}}{z}$, where $w, x, y, z$ are nonnegative integers.  What is $w + x + y + z$?

[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,P;
A=(0,5);
B=(8,5);
C=(8,0);
D=(0,0);
P=(3,5);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);
draw(P--D--B);
label("$A$",A,N);
label("$B$",B,N);
label("$C$",C,S);
label("$D$",D,S);
label("$P$",P,N);
[/asy]

Tangents are drawn from $(1,3)$ to the parabola $y^2 = 4x,$ at $A$ and $B.$  Find the length $AB.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

real upperparab (real x) {
  return (sqrt(4*x));
}

real lowerparab (real x) {
  return (-sqrt(4*x));
}

pair A, B, P;

P = (1,3);
A = ((7 + 3*sqrt(5))/2, upperparab((7 + 3*sqrt(5))/2));
B = ((7 - 3*sqrt(5))/2, upperparab((7 - 3*sqrt(5))/2));

draw(graph(upperparab,0,10));
draw(graph(lowerparab,0,10));
draw(interp(A,P,-0.8)--interp(A,P,1.2));
draw(interp(B,P,-1)--interp(B,P,1.5));

dot("$A$", A, N);
dot("$B$", B, W);
dot("$(1,3)$", P, NW);
[/asy]

Kite $ABCD$ (a quadrilateral with two pairs of adjacent equal sides) has coordinates $A\ (0,7),\ B\ (1,0),\ C\ (12,-2),$ and $D\ (7,8).$ What is the area of $ABCD,$ given that the area of a kite is equal to half the product of its diagonals?

[asy]
string sp(pair P, string P2){return "$" + P2 + "\,(" + string(P.x) + "," + string(P.y) + ")$";}
size(150); defaultpen(fontsize(10)); draw((-5,0)--(15,0),Arrows(4)); draw((0,-5)--(0,10),Arrows(4)); pair A=(0,7),B=(1,0),C=(12,-2),D=(7,8); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(0.7)); draw(A--C, dashed); draw(B--D, dashed); label(sp(A,"A"),A,W); label(sp(B,"B"),B,S); label(sp(C,"C"),C,E); label(sp(D,"D"),D,N);
[/asy]

For what ordered pair $(a,b)$ are there infinite solutions $(x,y)$ to the system \begin{align*}
3ax+3y&=5b,\\
2x+y&=5.
\end{align*}

Given that

\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{x}+\frac{1}{y}&=5,\\
3xy+x+y&=4,
\end{align*}

compute $x^2y+xy^2$.

Let \[f(n) =
\begin{cases}
4n+3 &\text{if }n<a, \\
7n-12 &\text{if }n\ge{a}.
\end{cases}
\]Find $a$ if the graph of $y=f(n)$ is continuous.

Line $l$ is a straight line. What is the value of $x$ in the diagram? [asy]
size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); import geometry;
draw(origin--(10,0),Arrows);
pair X = (5,0) + 5*dir(80);
draw((5,0)--X,EndArrow);
label("$x$",(5.4,0),NE);
label("$x+20^\circ$",(5,0),NW);
label("$l$",(0,0),NW);
[/asy]

In the diagram, the four points have coordinates $A(0,1)$, $B(1,3)$, $C(5,2)$, and $D(4,0)$.  What is the area of quadrilateral $ABCD$? [asy]
// draw axis
real low = -1; real high = 6;
draw((low, 0)--(high, 0), Arrow); draw((0, low)--(0, high - 1.5), Arrow);
label("$x$", (high, 0), E); label("$y$", (0, high - 1.5), N);

// draw quadrilateral
pair a = (0, 1); pair b = (1, 3); pair c = (5, 2); pair d = (4, 0);
draw(a--b--c--d--cycle);
label("$A$", a, W); label("$B$", b, N); label("$C$", c, E); label("$D$", d, S);
[/asy]

Carpet costs $\$21.95$ per square yard and the padding to put under it costs $\$2.55$ per square yard. Felix plans to install padding and carpet in the region shown in the diagram. What is the cost of the carpet and padding needed to exactly cover the room?

[asy]
unitsize(0.2 inch);
//import geometry;
draw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,2)--(4,2)--(4,5)--(0,5)--(0,0));

label("4 yds",(2,5),N);
